{
  "scope": {
    "what": [
      "The mock calendar-sync seed, as an outcome: what a seeded workspace contains.",
      "The dev command (db/dev/seed.rs) writes it into SQLite; the TS twin",
      "(apps/desktop/seeds/syncedCalendar.ts) builds it in MockStorageAdapter for test mode.",
      "Every shape here is the only way to reach some synced behaviour by hand, so a",
      "row that quietly disappears from one side costs the manual QA pass a check.",
      "Dates are structural: `day` is an offset from the run's local today, `monthEnd`",
      "is the last day of the run's local month, and both runners resolve them, so the",
      "table says nothing about the day it is run on.",
      "A calendar is named by a substring of its folder name, because only the display",
      "names differ (see excludes)."
    ],
    "excludes": [
      "Calendar/folder display names: the dev command names them 'Personal (synced)' and",
      "'Work (synced)' to stand apart from the realistic seed's own folders in the same",
      "dev database, while the mock's canned CalDAV discovery answers 'Personal' and",
      "'Work' and the seed cannot rename them. Matched by substring instead.",
      "sort_order values: the dev command numbers per folder from 0, the mock keeps one",
      "global counter. The order within a calendar is what QA sees, so `pageOrder` pins",
      "that and not the numbers.",
      "page_schedules rows for one-off mirrors: the dev command writes one per page, the",
      "mock keeps only the page's own denormalized schedule. Start/end are asserted on",
      "the page either way; the stored zone comes from whichever row holds it.",
      "sync_calendar.last_synced_at: the dev command stamps it so the panel reads fresh;",
      "the mock has no seam to stamp it from a seed.",
      "page_sync.user_modified: the dev command marks 'Team standup' owned because a",
      "parked description can only exist on a page the user has edited. The mock has no",
      "seam that stamps ownership from a seed (markPageSynced does not), and the",
      "calendar-sync e2e specs own a mirror by hand and count what teardown keeps, so",
      "closing this needs the mock seam and those specs, not the seed alone.",
      "pages.mirror_search_text: a dev-command column with no mock counterpart. The",
      "location and attendees it is built from are asserted instead."
    ]
  },
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "name": "one mock account owning two enabled calendars",
      "steps": [{ "op": "seed" }],
      "expect": {
        "account": {
          "displayName": "Mock Calendar (dev)",
          "provider": "caldav",
          "authKind": "basic"
        },
        "calendars": [
          { "name": "Personal", "color": "#7c9cf0", "enabled": true, "externalFolder": true },
          { "name": "Work", "color": "#f0a37c", "enabled": true, "externalFolder": true }
        ],
        "counts": {
          "accounts": 1,
          "calendars": 2,
          "calendarFolders": 2,
          "syncedPages": 15,
          "series": 7,
          "overrides": 3
        },
        "pageOrder": [
          {
            "calendar": "Personal",
            "titles": [
              "Team standup",
              "Design review (LA team)",
              "Company offsite",
              "Product summit",
              "Weekly 1:1 (London)",
              "Recurring review",
              "Swim class (term ends)"
            ]
          },
          {
            "calendar": "Work",
            "titles": [
              "Tokyo sync",
              "Budget sign-off",
              "Old planning (detached)",
              "Contractor call (no zone)",
              "Detached sprint",
              "Release countdown",
              "On-call rotation",
              "Month-end close"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "every one-off mirror, with its schedule, zone and read-only surface",
      "steps": [{ "op": "seed" }],
      "expect": {
        "pages": [
          {
            "title": "Team standup",
            "calendar": "Personal",
            "start": { "day": 0, "time": "11:00" },
            "end": { "day": 0, "time": "11:30" },
            "zone": "America/New_York",
            "syncState": "active",
            "location": "Zoom",
            "attendees": ["alex@example.com", "sam@example.com", "jordan@example.com"],
            "pendingDescription": "Agenda updated: demo the new sync panel, then round-table blockers.",
            "bodyText": "My prep: land the calendar-sync PR before we demo."
          },
          {
            "title": "Design review (LA team)",
            "calendar": "Personal",
            "start": { "day": 0, "time": "15:00" },
            "end": { "day": 0, "time": "16:00" },
            "zone": "America/Los_Angeles",
            "syncState": "active",
            "location": "Room 4B",
            "attendees": ["design@example.com"]
          },
          {
            "title": "Company offsite",
            "calendar": "Personal",
            "start": { "day": 0 },
            "end": null,
            "zone": null,
            "syncState": "active"
          },
          {
            "title": "Product summit",
            "calendar": "Personal",
            "start": { "day": 0 },
            "end": { "day": 2 },
            "zone": null,
            "syncState": "active"
          },
          {
            "title": "Tokyo sync",
            "calendar": "Work",
            "start": { "day": 1, "time": "10:00" },
            "end": { "day": 1, "time": "10:30" },
            "zone": "Asia/Tokyo",
            "syncState": "active"
          },
          {
